CIVIL 3D MCP CODE AUDIT FIXES
=============================
Date 2026-11-25
Base release 0.19.1 (changes are unreleased; version not bumped)

Scope
-----
This log records every code change made from the code audit of 2026-11-25: the
MCP server (Python), the bridge, the core helpers, every edit operation file
(plugin/Edit), every read action file (plugin/Read) and the part pickers
(plugin/Parts), plus the save-failure diagnostics and tests that came out of
it. Paths are relative to the project folder.

Each entry names the audit finding it answers and the check in
docs/AUDIT_TEST_PLAN.md that verifies it in Civil 3D.

Finding key
  H1-H8   high: H1 blocked event loop, H2 no progress on long calls,
          H3 re-entrant edits, H4 file-write surface, H5 pipe_set units,
          H6 part_swap scope, H7 block_import replace, H8 set_current styles
  M1-M16  medium: M1 request ledger cap, M2 dry run used up its request_id,
          M3 import reply handling, M4 bridge.json half-written, M5 QA
          undercount, M6 non-object operations, M7/M11 silent integer
          coercion, M8 tool description size, M9 cancellation, M10 shallow
          Clone(), M12 relative paths, M13 duplicate attribute tags,
          M14 unbounded replies, M15 silent pressure-part rename,
          M16 non-string items in name lists
  S1      save failure "object cannot be saved ... no file was created"
          (seen when quitting Civil 3D after the 0.15-0.19 live suites)
  C1      cleanup without behaviour change

Verification done before release
  - Compiled against the Civil 3D DLLs: 2027 (net10) and 2025 (net8) through
    tools/typecheck, and the real 2024 (net48) build of
    plugin/C3dMcpBridge.csproj. No new errors or warnings; the 12 obsolete-API
    warnings on 2027 are the same as before.
  - tests/smoke_test.py: ALL OK (includes the server against
    tests/fake_bridge.py, the catalogue/registry match and the docs check).
  - Server: offline check that tool schemas are unchanged, errors keep their
    text, a ping is answered during a slow call, and progress is sent.
  - tests/save_live.py: offline run against a fake bridge that breaks the
    drawing at the third edit.
  - Not yet run in Civil 3D: everything in docs/AUDIT_TEST_PLAN.md.


MCP SERVER (server/)
====================

01  server/server.py
--------------------
Added
  - _off_loop(): runs the blocking bridge call in a worker thread
    (anyio.to_thread.run_sync) and sends a progress notification every 10 s
    (HEARTBEAT_SECONDS) while it runs, when the client gave a progressToken.
  - A check that every item of params.operations is an object.
Removed
  - Synchronous tool functions.
Modified
  - civil3d, civil3d_read, civil3d_edit and civil3d_import are async and take
    the MCP Context (not part of the input schema; schemas are unchanged).
  - An exception from the bridge call is re-raised outside the task group, so
    the client sees the original message instead of "unhandled errors in a
    TaskGroup".
Why
  - H1: mcp 1.30 runs a synchronous tool directly on the event loop, so one
    edit (up to 630 s) froze the whole stdio session: no ping answers, no
    cancellation, every other request queued.
  - H2: the first edit waits on the permission dialog (up to 9 minutes) and
    imports take minutes; clients that time out requests (60 s in the
    TypeScript SDK) gave up while the edit could still be applied.
  - M6: non-object items passed the unknown-operation check and only failed
    in the plugin.
Test
  - A1, A2, A5.

