08  plugin/Bridge/EditRequests.cs
---------------------------------
Added
  - Order: insertion order of the request IDs.
  - EvictOldestFinished(): drops the oldest 10 % of completed or failed
    entries when the ledger is full; running entries stay.
  - Flag(): reads a true/false property of a reply and never throws.
Removed
  - The hard stop "This bridge session reached its edit request limit.
    Restart Civil 3D".
Modified
  - A dry run (dry_run: true) runs without being recorded.
  - "applied" and "afterCommitSucceeded" are read with Flag() instead of
    GetBoolean(), which threw on a missing or non-boolean value.
Why
  - M1: after 8192 edits in one session every edit was refused until Civil 3D
    was restarted.
  - M2: the fingerprint included dry_run, so the real edit with the dry run's
    request_id was refused as "a different edit".
Test
  - A4 (dry run then real edit); M1 needs no manual test.


CORE HELPERS (plugin/Core)
==========================

09  plugin/Core/J.cs
--------------------
Added
  - IndexParam(p, name, dflt, max): an optional 0-based index. Absent gives
    the default; anything that is not a whole number from 0 to max is
    refused (2.0 is accepted as 2).
  - NeedIndex(p, name, max): the same, required.
  - NameSet(p, name, max): a list of names as a case-insensitive set;
    numbers are taken as written.
  - NeedFullPath(p, name, op): checks that the path is fully qualified BEFORE
    Path.GetFullPath, then returns the full path.
Removed
  - None.
Modified
  - None (IntParam is unchanged and still used for limits and counts).
Why
  - M7/M11: IntParam returns the default for a wrong type and clamps out of
    range, so an index such as "2" or 2.5 silently became 0 and the edit hit
    the wrong object.
  - M12: callers ran Path.GetFullPath first, which turned a relative path into
    a path under Civil 3D's current folder and defeated the full-path check.
  - M16: e.GetString() threw a raw .NET message when a list held a number.
Test
  - C6, C7, C8.

