25  plugin/Read/SaveCheck.cs
----------------------------
Added
  - New file. diagnose_save (read only, the drawing is not changed):
    1. header: CLAYER, TEXTSTYLE, DIMSTYLE, CELTYPE, CMATERIAL, CMLEADERSTYLE,
       CTABLESTYLE, CDETAILVIEWSTYLE, CSECTIONVIEWSTYLE must point at live
       objects; CANNOSCALE must be in the annotation scale list;
    2. scan: every object (handles 1 to HANDSEED) is written with
       DBObject.DwgOut through ProbeFiler, a DwgFiler subclass that stores
       nothing (FileFiler by default, as a save; "copy" as an option).
       Objects whose writing throws or sets a filer error are listed, as are
       objects that write a hard owner or hard pointer to an erased or invalid
       object; soft pointers are counted, listed with soft_refs: true;
    3. save_copy: Database.Wblock() + SaveAs to %TEMP%, then the file is
       deleted.
    Also reports DBMOD, SAVETIME and SAVEFILEPATH.
Removed
  - None.
Modified
  - None.
Why
  - S1: the message gave no object or step. This check names the object
    (handle, type, owner, layer, Civil 3D name) and, run after each edit by
    tests/save_live.py, the edit that caused it. DwgOut and DwgFiler exist in
    the 2024, 2025 and 2027 APIs.
Risk
  - The probe filer is ours, not AutoCAD's. Confirmed in the live test: as a
    FileFiler it crashed Civil 3D 2027 (see 33); only the copy filer is used.
Test
  - E1-E6.


