AUDIT FINDINGS NOT CHANGED (and why)
====================================
H4  File writes after the one-time grant (save as / overwrite, points_export,
    plot_pdf, surface solids) can reach any folder; inspect_file reads any
    DWG without permission; the grant is per drawing, not per client.
    Not changed: allowed folders, extensions and per-client permission are a
    policy decision for the project owner.
H5  pipe_set "inner_diameter": the catalogue says catalogue units (mm), the
    API call uses drawing units (m) and snaps to the closest size.
    Not changed until D1 confirms which units the API takes.
H7  block_import replace: true also replaces same-named layers and styles.
    Not changed until D4 confirms; the fix (clear the block, clone its
    content with Ignore) changes the operation's behaviour.
H8  set_current of a style created in the same batch: after a rollback the
    current-style setting may point at an erased style. Not changed until D3
    (and E) confirm; diagnose_save reports it as a header problem.
M8  The tool description is about 40 KB. Not changed: shortening it changes
    what the assistant knows without calling help.
M9  Cancelling a call does not stop an edit already in Civil 3D (by design,
    so a batch is never left half done); check get_edit_status after a
    cancel.
--  pressure_network_erase may leave the parts (D2); surface_solids_create
    deletes the old file before writing (D7); network_interference on one
    pressure network reports pipes joined at fittings (D6); assembly_create
    may not chain subassemblies (D5); labels and section views are duplicated
    on a re-run (D8); surface_extract contours have no count limit.
    Not changed: each needs the Civil 3D behaviour confirmed first.
--  2027 obsolete-API warnings (ProfilePVI.Station, Part.AddToSectionView,
    Catchment members): working today; to be replaced in a later release.
--  Low findings (metric-only labels, dynamic block angles in radians, leader
    text style, description key set order, etc.): unchanged; listed in the
    audit report.


FIXES FROM THE LIVE TEST (2026-11-25, Civil 3D 2027)
===================================================

33  plugin/Read/SaveCheck.cs, server/catalog.py, tests/save_live.py
-------------------------------------------------------------------
Found
  - diagnose_save crashed Civil 3D 2027 (process gone, error report dialog)
    on the first call in an EMPTY drawing. tests/save_probe.py narrowed it:
    header check, the %TEMP% copy and a copy-filer scan of 5 objects pass;
    the scan with the default FileFiler crashes within the first 5 objects.
    Native objects written to a managed DwgFiler of type FileFiler expect
    AutoCAD's own file filer.
Removed
  - The "filer" option (file | copy) and the FileFiler default; --filer in
    save_live.py.
Modified
  - The scan always uses the copy filer; filer: "file" is refused with a
    message. The real save check is the %TEMP% copy (Wblock + SaveAs).
Added
  - tests/save_probe.py + run_save_probe.bat: steps through the stages of
    diagnose_save, logging each before it runs, so a crash names its stage.

34  plugin/Edit/ExtraOps.cs, plugin/Edit/EditContext.cs, plugin/Edit/EditEngine.cs
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Found (root cause of S1)
  - tests/run_save.bat: the drawing stays savable through the civil, data and
    geometry suites and extras edits 29-43; after extras edit #44
    (section_volume_tables) the three new AECC_SECTION_VIEW_QUANTITY_TAKEOFF_
    TABLE objects are open for write after the edit committed, minutes later
    and after REGEN. A real copy fails with eWasOpenForWrite, and quitting
    such a drawing ended once in "FATAL ERROR: Unhandled Access Violation".
  - tests/voltable_probe.py: every way of calling SectionView.VolumeTables.
    CreateVolumeTable leaves the table open (section view open for write in
    the edit's transaction, in a nested transaction, in an open-close
    transaction; total-volume and material tables). Opening the section view
    for read aborts Civil 3D (eNotOpenForWrite). Inside the edit's
    transaction the table is readable; the stray open appears when the
    transaction ends, also when it is rolled back. No extra transaction is
    left active. Opening the table for notify and closing it does not
    release it; asking that notify-opened object for DowngradeOpen (it
    reports eWasOpenForWrite) and then closing it does: the table is
    readable and a real copy of the drawing is written.
Added
  - EditContext.AfterEnd: work run once the batch's transaction is gone, on
    every path (committed, rolled back on an error, dry run), inside the
    document lock. EditEngine runs it (RunAfterEnd, never throws).
  - ExtraOps.ReleaseStrayOpens(): for each table section_volume_tables made,
    if it cannot be opened for read: open for notify, DowngradeOpen, Close
    (up to 3 times); a table that stays open is reported in the warnings
    (the drawing cannot be saved until Civil 3D is restarted).
Modified
  - section_volume_tables registers the release in AfterEnd.
  - diagnose_save also reports activeTransactions.
  - save_live.py counts objects that cannot be opened (left open by
    something else) in its one-line summary; before it said "0 object(s)
    fail to write".
Test
  - E1 (run_save.bat) must pass extras #44 and end SAVE CHECK CLEAN; then
    QUIT and answer No.

